  "summary": "Price moving with the trendline is the impulse: big departure candles, fast and easy to trade. Moving against it is the correction: small base candles, fake signals, risky. On H4 and below, trade only impulses. On the monthly, weekly and daily you may also trade corrections. A zone's purpose is to reach its target. Once the target has been reached, the zone will hold for only one or two candles on its next test and then break. An impulse often measures about 2.5x the previous correction.",
